    "assistant_ramble_edit_title": "Edit ramble transaction",
    "assistant_tutorial_title": "Transaction assistant",
    "assistant_tutorial_body": "<p>Easily create transactions by typing text here (or using your phone's dictation).</p>\n<p>Expected format:<br> <b>[search]&nbsp; [amount?]&nbsp; [description?]&nbsp; [todo?]</b></p>\n<p>1. The <b>search</b> looks in the name of your tags, categories and transaction-templates. It supports entering just part of the name and even getting some of the letters wrong.<br><code> elct => electricity</code></p>\n<p>2. The <b>amount</b> supports mathematical expressions. Numbers separated by a space get automatically added up.</p>\n<p>3. The <b>description</b> is optional. Use this to overwrite the default tag name.</p>\n<p>4. The <b>todo</b> makes it easy to add the user defined \"todo-tag\" by appending a custom string(default \"!!\"). This can be changed in \"Settings\"</p>\n<p>5. The <b>date</b> can be moved relative to today by typing <code>+1d</code> / <code>-5d</code> (plus or minus that many days) anywhere in the text.</p>\n\n<p><b>Examples</b><br>\n\"electricity\" = tag<br>\n\"swimming\" = template <br><br>\n\n<code>\nelectricity 23<br> \nelc 12*2+33<br> \nelc 12+2*3 custom description<br> \nelc 25 !!<br>\nelc 25 -1d<br>\nswim<br> \n\n</code>\n</p>\n\n<p>6. In the top-right there is a <b>currency</b> picker which you can change on the fly or set a default from \"Settings\" -> \"Assistant\". When used this will treat the <b>amount</b> as that currency and will convert the final value into your selected account currency. This can be really useful when going abroad.</p>",
